258:## 11. Isolation in shared workspaces (preventing consensus theater)
259-
260-Agreement only means something if it was reached independently. When agents share a filesystem, independence is a property of permissions and logs, not of instructions.
261-
262:### 11.1 Enforced drafting isolation
263-
264-- Each author drafts in its own directory, and the author's process cannot read sibling directories. Enforce this with filesystem permissions, separate checkouts, or a sandbox read-allowlist.  
265-- A prompt line such as "do not open other drafts" is **not** isolation.  
266-- If enforcement is impossible, cap the packet's decision at Provisional and record the gap under Confounds.
267-
268:### 11.2 Seal and publish
269-
270-- When an author finishes, record the draft's content hash and UTC time in an append-only seal log.  
271-- Drafts move into the shared `proposals/` directory only after **all** drafts are sealed (publish-after-all). Reviews follow the same rule.  
272-- If a sealed artifact's hash later changes, that is a Class 3 breach.
273-
274:### 11.3 Orchestrator–author firewall
275-
276-If the Orchestrator also authors on a packet:
277-
278-- The prompt for its drafting process is fixed and hashed before any competitor output exists.  
279-- That process must not see competitor output (draft, log, or stdout) before its own draft is sealed.  
280-- After seeing competitor output, the Orchestrator authors nothing further for its own track on that packet. If rebuttals or revisions are needed, a fresh process does them, given only the published files.
281-
282:### 11.4 Prompt parity
283-
284-- Competing authors' prompts are instantiated from one template. File the diff between instances.  
285-- Instances may differ only in author identity, output location, and the roster settings declared in A.5. Reviewer prompts follow the same rule.
286-
287:### 11.5 When agreement counts
288-
289-Agreement between candidates counts as independent evidence only if both of these hold:
290-
291-1. §11.1–§11.4 held, and that can be shown from logs.  
292-2. The agreed point is not stated or implied by the shared brief.
293-
294-Agreement on a point the brief already frames (for example, an ordering supplied as context) is recorded as **framed agreement** and adds no weight. Each draft must name at least one serious alternative it rejected, with the reason. When drafts converge on the same conclusion and also reject the same alternatives, the adjudicator records that as possible framing-driven convergence.
295-
296:### 11.6 Auditability
297-
298-- Every agent process that can read files runs with tool-call logging enabled.  
299-- Before publication, run a breach audit: search each author's tool log for sibling paths. Zero hits are required.  
300-- If a process has no tool log, its isolation is recorded as **unauditable**, and §6 rule 7 applies.
