305-
306:### 12.1 Who writes what
307-
308-| Artifact | Writer | Notes |
309-|---|---|---|
310-| Brief | Orchestrator, before Step 2 | Afterwards: appended amendments only (§10.4). Class 2 needs human signature |
311-| `roster.md` | Orchestrator, before Step 2 | Frozen afterwards |
312-| Author drafts | That author, inside its own sealed directory, or by mechanical deposit (§12.3) | Nobody else reads them until publish-after-all |
313-| `reviews/` | Each reviewer, its own file | Published together |
314-| Scores in `decision.md` | The bound adjudicator(s) | The Orchestrator may format the file but not alter scores |
315-| `spikes/<id>/PLAN.md` | Orchestrator, before execution | Hashed into the seal log |
316-| `spikes/<id>/` (everything else) | Experiment runner | Code, configs, raw outputs, `runs.log`, `deviations.md`, `BLOCKED.md` |
317-| Claim records | Claim author proposes. State changes only per B.9 | |
318-| `method-issues/` | Anyone | New files only |
319-| `logs/` | Each process writes its own files | Append-only (§12.4) |
320-| Program ledger | Orchestrator, at lock or pause | Append-only (§13.2) |
321-
322-Writing outside one's own rows is a process defect and must be filed (§10.2), even when it is harmless.
