679-- 2026-10-23: **v1.0.** Version header and pinning (entries above are v0). New §10: method issues, freeze set, amendment classes 0–3, contest-neutrality test, run retrospective. New §11: enforced isolation, seal and publish-after-all, Orchestrator–author firewall, prompt parity, conditions under which agreement counts. New §12: write-permission matrix, Experiment-runner code bounds, mechanical deposits and transcripts, append-only logs. New §13: program ledger, inheritance by ID, provisional cap, dependency propagation, pause/resume, step budgets. §4 Step 4: gates before ranking, independent and order-swapped adjudication, tie definition, Confounds paragraph. §6 rules 7–9. Appendix A: Orchestrator–adjudicator contradiction resolved, A.3 rules 6–7, new A.5 roster contract (model, effort, tools, parity). Appendix B: operational Grade-2 realization, challenge admissibility, new B.8 (capability ladders) and B.9 (claim governance). Motivated by process defects found in a live run: isolation enforced only by prompt, failure evidence overwritten on retry, an unversioned brief amendment, adjudicator role conflicts, and unequal author resources.

